    "id": "p9-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Draw a diagram and prove that, in a parallelogram, opposite sides are equal and opposite angles are equal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Opposite sides and opposite angles are equal.",
      "worked": "Draw diagonal AC in parallelogram ABCD. Since $AB\\parallel CD$ and $BC\\parallel AD$, $\\angle BAC=\\angle DCA$ and $\\angle BCA=\\angle DAC$ (alternate angles), and AC is common. Hence $\\triangle ABC\\cong\\triangle CDA$ by AAS. Thus $AB=CD$, $BC=DA$ and $\\angle ABC=\\angle CDA$. Also $\\angle BAD=\\angle BAC+\\angle CAD=\\angle DCA+\\angle ACB=\\angle BCD$. Therefore both pairs of opposite sides and angles are equal.",
